From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SheepyLord <37598021+SheepyLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:50:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the mod loader's texture reads between starts

At every start a USD mod's material walk opened each texture its
materials name to parse the DDS headers (findAsset), and again to copy
the five smallest mips a new texture uploads first, for every material
naming the file. The field's mods name about 25,500 textures in 16,700
files; a game start in the PoC spent 90 to 95 percent of the
"Loading enhancements" time in those opens (27 s with freshly deployed
mods, the rest of the walk under 2 s).

The mod texture cache keeps, per mod, what those reads produce: the
headers as the partial DDS loader parses them and the bytes of the
smallest mips, in rtx-remix\cache\mod-textures\<mod>-<hash>.bin.
- An entry is used only while its file has the same size, last write
  time, change time and NTFS file id, from one folder listing per
  texture folder (FileIdBothDirectoryInfo); the file is not opened.
- A file read afresh is kept only when the file itself, opened for its
  attributes alone, matches the listing and has one name (a hard-linked
  file's folder entry can be stale); folders, links and file systems
  without change times are always read.
- A miss reads the file once: the tail read for the cache also feeds the
  texture's first upload. Repeated names in one load share one asset.
- A cached asset is the partial loader's DdsTextureData restored from the
  record, so its hash, info and larger mips (read from the file on
  demand) are the same; the kept mips serve data() until uploaded.
- The file (magic, version, FNV-1a checksum) is written only when the load
  used anything else than it read, atomically; a damaged or foreign one
  is ignored and rewritten. Hot reloads read files as before.

rtx.initializer.modTextureCache (default True) turns it off.

[RTX Mod Load] lines give each mod's first load (stage, materials with
their USD, find and texture times, meshes, lights) and the whole load;
[RTX Mod Texture Cache] lines give each mod's hits and misses.

rtx_mod_texture_store.h is self-contained, and
tests/rtx/unit/test_mod_texture_store.cpp tests it with real files
(the GMod native loader project's gate compiles it from this patch).
